                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e054817b-1152-4174-8205-3f235355e96f",
                        "source_entry_id": "da9bc334-5374-31a6-b288-b6df4d580996",
                        "source_sense_id": "20690609-6066-3e2f-bdda-805c258dd4d7",
                        "target_lang_word": "gosling",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "gosling",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "29cedec2-56fc-3cbb-86fc-a1bbf744849a",
                                        "entry_id": "71121d2f-0913-356a-94d7-e42498ea8638",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A young goose."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "33eb3da0-70af-47da-bf6f-89d22d6279dc",
                                                "sense_id": "29cedec2-56fc-3cbb-86fc-a1bbf744849a",
                                                "text": "Marta's gander was a magnificent snow-white bird: the object of terror to foxes, children and dogs. She had reared him as a gosling; and whenever he approached, he would let fly a low contented burble and sidle his neck around her thighs."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0eba30d9-a812-3801-9e27-fa1d08ee3f0a",
                                        "entry_id": "71121d2f-0913-356a-94d7-e42498ea8638",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An inexperienced and immature, or foolish and naive, young person."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0fbc4896-0cd0-4263-afd2-901efc45cec4",
                                                "sense_id": "0eba30d9-a812-3801-9e27-fa1d08ee3f0a",
                                                "text": "Two stout woodmen with difficulty cut down this tree, the chips of which flew far and wide about the hall; but at my command my two green goslings carried away the fragments without any difficulty."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "808a787f-a066-39cb-b7fb-f3213883820b",
                                        "entry_id": "71121d2f-0913-356a-94d7-e42498ea8638",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A catkin on willows, nut trees, and pines."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "88da89df-ab0e-485e-be17-0a0a5e12cd3b",
                                                "sense_id": "808a787f-a066-39cb-b7fb-f3213883820b",
                                                "text": "These Aments (we must no longer call them catkins) are composed both of male and female flowers; what Henry calls goslings in spring are the Aments of the willow tree ; his green goslings are female Aments , and , when mature , have the appearance of little tufts of wool, which appearance is caused by the downy material that crowns their feeds;"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "28c3ca29-7093-4463-9344-ecfba6cab167",
                                                "sense_id": "808a787f-a066-39cb-b7fb-f3213883820b",
                                                "text": "When the oak puts on his goslings grey 'Tis time to sow barley night or day."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6efccb17-f199-4de3-bca6-4a3182865256",
                                                "sense_id": "808a787f-a066-39cb-b7fb-f3213883820b",
                                                "text": "The common Sallow or Goat Willow (Salix caprea) forms a small bush in rough places and the hollows left by old gravel-pits. It produces the “goslings” which children are fond of gathering at Easter ."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f844b127-4a34-4a34-a5a9-8acb7c946611",
                                                "sense_id": "808a787f-a066-39cb-b7fb-f3213883820b",
                                                "text": "In the afternoon: cut back the crack willow around the pool; the fluffy flowers fall on the water. Locally, the flowers are known as 'goslings'. Water. It has no motion of its own; it is the mechanic betrayer of other forces. the breeze gently drifts the goslings to the far shore."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a0ecd26f-0e05-4b24-8fd9-acb28d577eb4",
                        "source_entry_id": "da9bc334-5374-31a6-b288-b6df4d580996",
                        "source_sense_id": "20690609-6066-3e2f-bdda-805c258dd4d7",
                        "target_lang_word": "house",
                        "target_lang_code": "cs",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "house",
                                "target_lang_code": "cs",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "01770818-ca27-31c4-bafc-b274c039936f",
                                        "entry_id": "a78ca8f4-3886-3a5e-82c9-1e141efff711",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "mládě husy"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "08bf664c-6d58-4e60-8bf5-fff4c27beaee",
                                                "sense_id": "01770818-ca27-31c4-bafc-b274c039936f",
                                                "text": "Housata pobíhala kolem své mámy."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4f72c838-60af-333e-8cf6-8f6ccb484a0f",
                                        "entry_id": "a78ca8f4-3886-3a5e-82c9-1e141efff711",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "mladá nezkušená osoba"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "18dea778-38a3-40ff-aeed-d0bf232e15b1",
                                                "sense_id": "4f72c838-60af-333e-8cf6-8f6ccb484a0f",
                                                "text": "Tenkrát jsem byl ještě slévačské house."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "house",
                                "target_lang_code": "cs",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cab50aa6-6953-3094-becf-cdf01ec8fcac",
                                        "entry_id": "9cea46da-8398-3ff9-a7f5-a6aa7d4f4cba",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "taneční hudební styl"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b96d961e-3e54-4e6f-a1e2-3ed8be25825f",
                                                "sense_id": "cab50aa6-6953-3094-becf-cdf01ec8fcac",
                                                "text": "House poslouchám nerad."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "42923938-5084-4d0d-9ebd-d425c7b42691",
                        "source_entry_id": "da9bc334-5374-31a6-b288-b6df4d580996",
                        "source_sense_id": "20690609-6066-3e2f-bdda-805c258dd4d7",
                        "target_lang_word": "oison",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "oison",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b3c83034-e892-3ca3-8dff-d1d868324e23",
                                        "entry_id": "169e3a32-5564-3f24-9eec-5827c8ad88bc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Le petit d’une oie"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2ce6605f-3704-48c5-a9d4-0472b9c19e93",
                                                "sense_id": "b3c83034-e892-3ca3-8dff-d1d868324e23",
                                                "text": "Un jeune oison."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "be124614-021d-40b6-bbc5-b8c10e87baea",
                                                "sense_id": "b3c83034-e892-3ca3-8dff-d1d868324e23",
                                                "text": "Un petit oison."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "43ef659a-4bb4-4d15-b939-eb1daacacfa2",
                                                "sense_id": "b3c83034-e892-3ca3-8dff-d1d868324e23",
                                                "text": "Oison bridé",
                                                "translation": "celui à qui l’on a placé une plume dans les ouvertures qui sont à la partie supérieure du bec, pour l’empêcher d’entrer dans les lieux fermés de haies."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1abad494-a025-4cda-83a1-1cf876618b00",
                                                "sense_id": "b3c83034-e892-3ca3-8dff-d1d868324e23",
                                                "text": "Elle manquait bien un peu d’adresse aussi. Par exemple elle ne savait pas faire manger les oisons dans sa main, les forcer devant leur pâtée de son et d’orties."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e56750a9-0e49-4d64-8c92-946f91d131b4",
                                                "sense_id": "b3c83034-e892-3ca3-8dff-d1d868324e23",
                                                "text": "Mary Wiggins attend l’éclosion de trois œufs d’oie, et se désespère lorsqu’un seul donne naissance à un oison presque moribond."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3501c27a-ffad-49e8-8fa1-bd8a64a18450",
                                                "sense_id": "b3c83034-e892-3ca3-8dff-d1d868324e23",
                                                "text": "Mais concluant je dis et maintiens, qu’il n’y a tel torchecul que d’un oison bien duveté, pourvu qu’on lui tienne la tête entre les jambes. Et m’en croyez sur mon honneur. Car vous sentez au trou du cul une volupté mirifique, tant par la douceur d’icelui duvet, que par la chaleur tempérée de l’oison, laquelle facilement est communiquée au boyau culier et autres intestins, jusqu’à venir à la région du cœur et du cerveau."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "334b83a5-e5dc-3878-9484-0e3f9c7f9272",
                                        "entry_id": "169e3a32-5564-3f24-9eec-5827c8ad88bc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Par dérision, il se dit d’un homme niais et sot à qui l’on fait croire tout ce que l’on veut."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "90e90dfd-d2a7-4086-98c1-1ec64ba3fe9c",
                                                "sense_id": "334b83a5-e5dc-3878-9484-0e3f9c7f9272",
                                                "text": "« Il faut déjà le comble de l’abnégation et de l’adresse pour mener vingt-huit de ces oisons-là, pensait M. Leuwen, que serait-ce s’ils étaient quarante ou cinquante, et encore des gens d’esprit, dont chacun voudrait être mon lieutenant, et bientôt évincer son capitaine ? »"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5e534862-f202-4f98-911d-a57239c36fe8",
                                                "sense_id": "334b83a5-e5dc-3878-9484-0e3f9c7f9272",
                                                "text": "Je tiens le pari ! cria le noble oison."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4e715e88-2d06-4224-9176-92667d0f33e2",
                                                "sense_id": "334b83a5-e5dc-3878-9484-0e3f9c7f9272",
                                                "text": "– Il s’est laissé plumer comme un oison."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
